text.en:
(1) The duties of the Board shall be -

(a) to investigate whether any provisions of this Order has been or is being contravened;

(b) to make recommendations to the Permanent Secretary on the enforcement of any provision of this Order; and

(c) generally to do all such acts and things as are necessary to be carried out under the provisions of this Order.

(2) For the purpose of performing its duties under this Order, the Board may -

(a) hear and examine witnesses on oath;

(b) summon any person to attend any hearing of the Board to give evidence or produce any document or other article in his possession;

(c) generally require any person to furnish any information or produce any document or other article in his possession;

(d) require any person to attend any counselling or mediation session as the Board may specify; and

(e) do anything incidental to any of its powers.

(3) The Minister may give such directions, not inconsistent with the provisions of this Order, as to the exercise of the powers and the performance of the duties of the Board and the Board shall give effect to any such directions. Penalties.
